draw(shift(0.75,2)*p, (0,1)--(1,1), EndArrow);
draw(shift(2.25,2)*p, (1,1)--(2,1), EndArrow);
draw(shift(1.5,4)*p, (1.5,3)--(1.5,4), EndArrow);
[/asy] There are six ordered triples of numbers from the members of $\{1, 2, 3\}$, are ${123, 213, 213, 213, 231, 231}$.  The first, second, and fourth form the same numbers as the target, and the last two share a value to be added.  We must also requre that, in these cases, the number being used last must be larger than the first number in the triplet.  The first and fourth can form anything from $\{2, 3, 2, 3, 2, 3\}$, but the other two times we must have the number $3$.  The maximum is made by using 2,2,3 and the minimum by using 1,2,3.  Hence, the answer is $333-213=120$.

